Data built into the server:

  GeoNames place names               Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
                                     (CC BY 4.0), https://www.geonames.org/
                                     third_party/geonames/PROVENANCE.md

    The towns photo places are named after (ADR 0078), trimmed to the fields
    LANcast uses and embedded so that naming a place asks nobody's server.

Built by this project and shipped beside the client:

  libmpv (mpv, FFmpeg, libplacebo,   GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1
  dav1d, shaderc, SPIRV-Cross,       or later, as configured
  zlib)                              third_party/libmpv/PROVENANCE.md

    Built from pinned sources with mpv's -Dgpl=false and FFmpeg without
    --enable-gpl, so the result is LGPL rather than GPL (ADR 0069). It is
    loaded at runtime by full path and never linked, so replacing the file
    replaces the library. The recipe that builds it, and the exact source
    revisions, are in third_party/libmpv/.

